{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c577","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a9c5-2eb3-7902-83b0-77aeb115d140"},"sequence":278,"recorded_at":1780531400000551,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0bd83bfa-ae0a-4313-a4d0-115d5a67d246","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"0bd83bfa-ae0a-4313-a4d0-115d5a67d246","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0bd83bfa-ae0a-4313-a4d0-115d5a67d246"},"call_id":"call_01a0a9c5e7a572de8894efdd72817957","text":"Read text file `/tmp/r4/logbook-rev3.md`.\n1|# TASK-260916-304bw2 — reviewer logbook, revision 3\n2|\n3|Exact candidate debeb04099cfb7e7cd7374ed1e993d092c943bf3. Six prior focused regressions pass. Three new production-entry probes fail with five assertions. Same-account re-login through real GitHubAuth.Flow defeats account-based continuity: old Apply resumes authenticated work/publication and old unregister executes removal. Relink rewrites the catalog scope, allowing an old editor to PUT to another organization. These repeat R2-F1/F2/F3, so retain named regressions plus narrowing mutants in the owning leaf. Coherent session incarnation must distinguish login replacement from token refresh; original editor identity must survive mutable catalog/disk changes. No production mutations or product-code edits. Verdict changes_requested; no human blocker.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c579","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a9c5-2eb3-7902-83b0-77aeb115d140"},"sequence":279,"recorded_at":1780531400000553,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0bd83bfa-ae0a-4313-a4d0-115d5a67d246","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"0bd83bfa-ae0a-4313-a4d0-115d5a67d246","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0bd83bfa-ae0a-4313-a4d0-115d5a67d246"},"call_id":"call_01a0a9c5e8cf7053b641c8a6e0343be2","text":"Read text file `/tmp/r4/r3-outcome.md`.\n1|# TASK-260916-304bw2 — R3 session-and-editor-binding rework (developer outcome)\n2|\n3|Status: ready for review (board `to-review`).\n4|\n5|Revision 3 adopts the three exact rev2 reviewer probes as maintained\n6|production-entry regressions and fixes R2-F1–F3 at the root cause with one\n7|coherent immutable operation/session ownership boundary: every mutating\n8|catalog operation captures the catalog generation plus the initiating\n9|GitHub session once, and re-checks both at every asynchronous boundary\n10|through confirmation and publication — never only before the side effect.\n11|Accepted registration/global installer lease, stopped-only unregister,\n12|distinct service identities, fail-closed persistence, corrected real login\n13|policy, and the existing repository editor are preserved. No production\n14|runner was stopped, re-registered, or interrupted; the candidate is left\n15|UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for handoff snapshot.\n16|\n17|## Fixes by finding\n18|\n19|### R2-F1 — editor/write authority bound to the catalog original\n20|- `Runners.Flow.verifiedOrgRunner` (extended): the mutable on-disk\n21|  registration must still agree with the server host and org scope\n22|  recorded at import (or explicit relink). A same-host scope edit on disk\n23|  without re-verification refuses with a message naming both scopes,\n24|  instead of silently retargeting another org's group.\n25|- Load and Apply both verify here, so neither path can drift off the\n26|  catalog original between Load and Apply; `bindApplyIdentity` keeps\n27|  guarding across awaits within Apply. Entries without a recorded\n28|  server/scope predate the binding and fall through to the unchanged\n29|  disk-vs-session checks (stated bound).\n30|- Explicit re-verification path: remove + re-add (or relink of a moved\n31|  folder) rebinds the original; proven by\n32|  `scopeEditThenReAddReverifiesGroupApply`, which then PUTs to\n33|  `orgs/other-org/` only.\n34|\n35|### R2-F2 — session ownership carried through completion (Apply + Load)\n36|- `Runners.Flow.applyGroupAccess`: after the PUT, a logout/account/server\n37|  switch refuses the confirmation read and any `groupAccessLoaded`\n38|  publication (the already-issued PUT is not pretended undoable).\n39|- `Runners.Flow.loadGroupAccess` (sibling completion): the same ownership\n40|  guards sit before the repository fetch and before publication.\n41|- Error completions in both paths publish only when the starting session\n42|  still holds; mid-operation session loss stops silently, matching the\n43|  existing pre-PUT and `refreshRemote` shape. Never-authenticated\n44|  callers still get their `notAuthenticated` failure (started=nil,\n45|  current=nil still owns).\n46|\n47|### R2-F3 — unregister bound to the initiating session, state always released\n48|- `Runners.Flow.runUnregister` (new, split from `unregister`): captures\n49|  the initiating session once; a logout/account/server switch after\n50|  token acquisition — and again at the side-effect boundary — invalidates\n51|  the unstarted `config.sh remove` (minted token expires unused) while\n52|  the stopped and local-identity gates stay intact.\n53|- Local bookkeeping after a *completed* side effect still runs: a remote\n54|  removal that already happened is real even if the session changed\n55|  under the installer lease, and no cancellation undoes it.\n56|- The split guarantees the epilogue: every early return still clears\n57|  `unregisterWorking` and publishes `unregistering(id, false)`, so an\n58|  invalidated attempt never wedges the UI and a retry proceeds (this\n59|  also repairs the latent wedge on the pre-existing catalog-stale early\n60|  returns). Proven by `unregisterReleasesOperationStateAfterSessionLoss`.\n61|\n62|## Production call sites\n63|\n64|| Fix | Call site |\n65||---|---|\n66|| R2-F1 | `Runners.Flow.apply(.applyGroupAccess/.loadGroupAccess)` → `verifiedOrgRunner` catalog-original check → `GitHubRunnerAPIClient.setGroupRepositories` |\n67|| R2-F2 | `Runners.Flow.apply(.applyGroupAccess)` → `sessionStill` post-PUT + pre-publish → `fetchGroupRepositories` / `groupAccessLoaded`; same in `loadGroupAccess` |\n68|| R2-F3 | `Runners.Flow.apply(.unregister)` → `runUnregister` post-token + boundary `sessionStill` → `RunnerInstallerService.unregister` |\n69|\n70|## Tests: 6 new, 216 total green\n71|\n72|Adopted probes (failed exit 1 with 5 assertion failures on rev2, pass now):\n73|`reviewR2ScopeEditAfterLoadMustNotRetargetApply`,\n74|`reviewR2LogoutDuringPutMustNotPublishAccess`,\n75|`reviewR2LogoutDuringRemoveTokenMustRefuseSideEffect`.\n76|\n77|New bounds: `loadGroupAccessStopsPublishingAfterMidLoadLogout` (sibling\n78|Load completion), `unregisterReleasesOperationStateAfterSessionLoss`\n79|(retry after invalidation), `scopeEditThenReAddReverifiesGroupApply`\n80|(refusal names drift + explicit re-verification PUTs to the new org only).\n81|\n82|AC coverage: 18 of 19 named rows driven through production entry points\n83|(row 18, full UI paths, remains the stated manual-UI bound; no UI tests\n84|per task). Findings touched rows 11/16 and the async/session contract.\n85|\n86|## Mutant evidence: 4 narrowing, 0 survivors\n87|\n88|Tree reverted after each run (grep-verified clean); full suite re-run\n89|green afterwards. Each mutant keeps the gate present and weakens it to\n90|admit exactly one rejected subclass; a retained-gate control still passes.\n91|\n92|| Mutant | Narrows the gate to | Named failing test | Exit |\n93||---|---|---|---|\n94|| `verify-admits-scope-drift` | Catalog binding keeps host + agent checks, drops scope-vs-original | `reviewR2ScopeEditAfterLoadMustNotRetargetApply` (PUT emitted); `reviewCrossServerGroupApplyMustRefuse` still passes | 1 |\n95|| `apply-completion-admits-logout` | Session ownership keeps pre-PUT checks, admits post-PUT logout at confirmation + publication | `reviewR2LogoutDuringPutMustNotPublishAccess` (2 issues: published + 4th request); `applyGroupAccessStopsWhenSessionChangesMidApply` still passes | 1 |\n96|| `unregister-admits-post-token-logout` | Unregister keeps stopped + local-identity gates, admits post-token logout at both session points | `reviewR2LogoutDuringRemoveTokenMustRefuseSideEffect` (2 issues: installer ran + ID cleared); `unregisterRefusesRunningService` + `unregisterRevalidatesStoppedAtSideEffectBoundary` still pass | 1 |\n97|| `load-completion-admits-logout` | Load keeps membership verification, admits mid-Load logout at repos fetch + publication | `loadGroupAccessStopsPublishingAfterMidLoadLogout` (2 issues); `groupAccessUsesFreshAPIMembershipNotStalePool` still passes | 1 |\n98|\n99|No survivors. No delete-only rows claimed as narrowing.\n100|\n101|## Validation (real exit codes)\n102|\n103|- `swift test --package-path Packages/RunnerControlCore` → exit 0, 216\n104|  tests passed (210 R2 + 6 R3), re-run green after mutant reverts.\n105|- `python3 -m unittest discover -s Scripts/tests` → exit 0, 62 tests OK\n106|  (release machinery untouched).\n107|- `./Scripts/build.sh` → exit 0, `BUILD SUCCEEDED`;\n108|  `codesign --verify --deep --strict` → exit 0 (inside build.sh);\n109|  `1.2.0`, `works.relux.runnercontrol`, team `262RZ595FP`, fresh\n110|  candidate in `.temp/products/`.\n111|- No configured linter (no SwiftLint config); build shows only the\n112|  pre-existing Sendable-closure warnings pattern, none in changed files.\n113|- Production (read-only): `macbook-iv` service `state = running`,\n114|  exactly one `runsvc.sh` + one `Runner.Listener` per runner\n115|  (macbook-iv, cocoaskills); no `actions.runner.*` in\n116|  `~/Library/LaunchAgents` (manual external login OFF preserved).\n117|\n118|## Stated bounds\n119|\n120|- UI confirmation paths are manual (root CUA on the fresh candidate; no\n121|  UI tests per task). The production Flow gates behind them are covered.\n122|- An in-flight membership page loop may finish its current read after a\n123|  mid-loop logout; no write, confirmation read, or publication follows\n124|  (in production the next read 401s and the error completion is\n125|  suppressed by the same ownership check).\n126|- Catalog entries without a recorded server/scope predate the R2-F1\n127|  binding and rely on the disk-vs-session checks.\n128|- Concurrent wizard + catalog edits to the same group remain\n129|  last-write-wins (rev1 bound, unchanged).\n130|- A remove token minted just before a session invalidation expires\n131|  unused; the refused side effect is `config.sh remove` (proven\n132|  installer-idle).","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
